# Gitignored files copied into a new Claude Code worktree.
#
# A worktree is a fresh checkout, so gitignored files are absent from it.
# Claude Code copies the entries below when it creates a worktree — via
# `claude --worktree`, `moai cc|glm|cg -w`, or a subagent spawned with
# `isolation: worktree`.
#
# Syntax is .gitignore syntax. Only files that BOTH match a pattern here AND
# are gitignored get copied; tracked files are never duplicated.
#
# NOT processed when a custom WorktreeCreate hook replaces the default git
# behavior — copy local files inside that hook instead.
#
# Add your own project-local files below (local overrides, build caches your
# toolchain needs) using the same .gitignore syntax. Do not list secrets —
# .env files, private keys, credentials: every new worktree, including each
# subagent's, would get its own copy of them (Issue #2670).

# .claude/settings.local.json is deliberately not listed. In GLM mode the
# session-start hook writes ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN into it, so copying it would
# put the token into every new worktree (Issue #2670). If a worktree session
# needs per-machine settings such as env.PATH, create
# .claude/settings.local.json in that worktree by hand.
